## Radical Innovation (advisory)

Rebuild Post 1's middle around the five stand-ins that its own lesson line already names: a photo for a measurement, one bulb for the standard, a word for a shape, a guess for a probe, a label for a fact. That would mean five sections in place of the current sections 2 through 7. Each section would tell one episode with three parts:

- the stand-in that crossed the gap;
- how the other half caught it;
- the real thing that crossed instead, with the print or photo that proved it.

Before "Wall on Both Sides", one compact "stand-in ledger" table would hold the remaining episodes with these columns: stand-in, what it replaced, who caught it, what crossed instead. The prose would then carry five episodes and the table the rest. This answers the sprawl risk and the "highlight reel" pre-mortem, since every section serves the lesson by construction. It would also bring the post near 2,500 words without losing an episode. The cost is redoing the section outline in the beat sheet; the sources and quotes stay the same.
